  "body": "Follow-up to your3a29cb8 final-tail implementation on candidate/api-plan-simple. Focused commit **f82d46c**; actual counter fixtures reproduce busy-load and steal findings becoming quiet when the last window is replaced.\n\nExample:0->1s observes110 CPU ticks (1.10 CPUs, busy). A0.4s quiet tail adds no ticks. Replacing that window from its original baseline produces785 milli-CPUs; `describe(windows)` becomes quiet. The steal channel has the same failure. Once-only extension protects repeated snapshots, but a single extension can already erase this finding.\n\nThe safeguard keeps an already-busy window intact; that run already has no speed verdict. Quiet windows still extend and newly busy tails still flag. No shorter counter intervals, new threshold, hashing or statistics change. The join body was extracted unchanged for deterministic counter fixtures; fixtures use production `between`, `Window::busy`, and `describe`.\n\nEvidence: https://github.com/devonjonte/bench-hashes/blob/1da9222/audit/results/current-rust-gate/README.md . Both new preservation controls fail before (exit101); four focused controls pass after.16 clocks tests pass/1ignored. Bounded standard perf check using your NEW Rust regress path passes after two pairs/all14points. Both sides use current instrument: no instrumentation-overhead or reliability claim. Linux tested; native Mac remains untested.\n\nI recorded your T1\u2013T8 response and am adapting remaining validation to the sole Rust reader/fast-median decision path. Historical q5 data retains its old-source scope. NO-GO remains pending current-detector calibration.",
